{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-confinement-phase-stratification","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:confinement-phase-stratification","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of confinement phase stratification","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-confinement-phase-stratification"],"text":"confinement-phase-stratification-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:confinement-phase-stratification\"></a><p><em>Claim (1)—Openness.</em>\n<em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S := \\{(q, X) : \\forall i,\\ 0 &#x3C; g_i(q, X)\\}</code>. Each set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{0 &#x3C; g_i\\}</code> is open because <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g_i</code> is continuous, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I</code> is finite, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S</code> is open. <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega(P)</code> is the image of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S</code> under the projection <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(q, X) \\mapsto q</code>, which is an open map. Hence <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega(P)</code> is open.</em></p>\n<p><em>Claim (2)—Constancy on a phase.</em>\n<em>Fix <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda</code>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U := \\{q : u^*_\\lambda(q) > 0\\}</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V := \\{q : s_\\lambda(q) > 0\\}</code>; both are open by continuity. Strict complementarity gives <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">C \\subseteq U \\cup V</code>. If <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">C</code> met both <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V</code>, then, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">C</code> being connected, it would meet <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U \\cap V</code> at some <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>; there <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u^*_\\lambda(q)\\, s_\\lambda(q) > 0</code>, contradicting complementarity. So either <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u^*_\\lambda > 0</code> on all of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">C</code>, or <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u^*_\\lambda > 0</code> nowhere on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">C</code>. This holds for every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda</code>, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}^*(P, q)</code> is the same set for every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in C</code>, and so is its size <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mu(P, q)</code>. <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\square</code></em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/confinement-phase-stratification-proof.md","heading":"Proof","page":"b/prf-confinement-phase-stratification","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":25,"unknown":0,"stale":82},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
